      "message": "OOC, what causes current.api to show \"carrier privileges\" instead of the constant variable name like it does for READ_PHONE_STATE and other manifest permissions? That seems slightly cleaner, but not a huge deal.\n\nOn the other hand, one of the things we\u0027ve been talking about for S has been the possibility of defining a new permission that is required for carrier apps to declare in order to access carrier-privileged APIs. It\u0027s functionally no different but allows for auditing / clearer use of the permission model for carrier privileged APIs. This feels like a step in the right direction either way, but we might end up just adding a regular permission anyway, so we should be cautious about doing substantially more work than this.",
