      "writtenOn": "2020-12-02T21:23:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The @RequiresPermission annotation itself is not actually part of the SDK and doesn\u0027t show up anywhere consequential.\n\nIt\u0027s used to signal the documentation generator tool that it needs to include some pre-formatted text. In the case of @RequiresPermission(\"carrier privileges\"), it auto-generates documentation that looks like this: `Requires {@link android.telephony.TelephonyManager#hasCarrierPrivileges carrier privileges}`\n\nSee ag/906597 for some other more complete examples.\n\nSDK documentation is not translated either fwiw.",
      "parentUuid": "4d8ec02e_93531c67",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 174,
